{%- doc -%}
  Echoes a product name with its shouting words set in title case.

  The catalogue does not write its own names one way. Thirty-seven of two hundred
  and seventeen are typed in full caps, and others shout only in the middle —
  "12-Pack of TEACHER'S APPRECIATION TREATS" — so a grid of them reads as a rash.

  The fix cannot be CSS. No rule turns "12 PACK GIFT BOX" back into "12 Pack Gift
  Box", because the lowercase that name needs is not in the string any more. Only
  Liquid can put it back.

  **Word by word, not name by name.** A first version rebuilt a name only when the
  whole of it shouted, which left the half-shouting ones exactly as they were —
  the very thing this is for.

  A word with a lowercase letter in it is never touched: somebody wrote it that
  way on purpose. What gets rebuilt is a word in full caps, unless it is:

  - an acronym or a code. `RD`, `WS`, `M&M`, `B+` and `TFL` are the ones this
    catalogue actually uses — read off the names that are otherwise properly
    written, where a capitalised word can only be deliberate. Guessing by length
    instead would have kept `BOX` and `OZ` shouting.
  - a small word. Title case leaves `of`, `and`, `with` lowercase unless they open
    the name: "Box of 12 Jumbo Bars", not "Box Of 12 Jumbo Bars".

  Hyphens break words as spaces do, or `12-PACK` comes back as `12-pack`.

  @param {string} title - The name to set.

  @example
  {% render 'ui-title-case', title: product.title %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign source = title | default: '' | strip

  # Spelled the way the shop's own properly-written names spell them.
  assign keep = 'RD>RD,WS>WS,OP>OP,M&M>M&M,M&MS>M&Ms,M&MS™>M&Ms™,B+>B+,TFL>TFL,NY>NY,USA>USA,SQF>SQF,PNC>PNC,XO>XO' | split: ','
  assign minor = 'of and with the a an in on for to or by at from' | split: ' '

  assign words = source | split: ' '
  assign out = ''
-%}
{%- for word in words -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign token = word | strip
    assign done = ''

    if token != blank
      assign upper = token | upcase
      assign lower = token | downcase

      # Not in full caps, or carrying no letters at all — leave it exactly as it is.
      if token != upper or upper == lower
        assign done = token
      else
        for pair in keep
          assign parts = pair | split: '>'
          if token == parts[0]
            assign done = parts[1]
            break
          endif
        endfor

        if done == blank
          if forloop.first == false and minor contains lower
            assign done = lower
          else
            assign chunks = lower | split: '-'
            for chunk in chunks
              assign raised = chunk | capitalize
              if forloop.first
                assign done = raised
              else
                assign done = done | append: '-' | append: raised
              endif
            endfor
          endif
        endif
      endif

      if out == blank
        assign out = done
      else
        assign out = out | append: ' ' | append: done
      endif
    endif
  -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- out -}}
